{"step_index":2179,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:05Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n7. Phase 5: Create a Problem Learning Workspace\n\nWhen a user opens a problem, display a dedicated learning page.\n\nA. Understand the Problem\n\nExplain the problem in simple English.\n\nShow:\n\nWhat the problem asks.\n\nInput and output examples.\n\nExpected output for each example.\n\nImportant constraints.\n\nEdge cases.\n\nWhat the learner needs to calculate or return.\n\nDo not immediately reveal the solution.\n\nB. Learn the Pattern\n\nExplain:\n\nWhich DSA pattern is relevant.\n\nWhy the pattern is useful.\n\nWhich prerequisite concepts are needed.\n\nA small illustrative example.\n\nA simple explanation of the intended approach.\n\nUse built-in, rule-based teaching content. Do not call an AI API.\n\nC. Try It Yourself\n\nProvide a Python editor where the user can write their own solution.\n\nInclude:\n\nRun Code.\n\nRun Tests.\n\nReset Code.\n\nShow Hints.\n\nReveal Reference Solution, with confirmation.\n\nView Test Results.\n\nUse a safe, restricted execution environment. Never execute unrestricted user code on the main application server.\n\nIf the existing execution infrastructure cannot safely support arbitrary Python, implement a restricted interpreter for supported syntax or clearly document the limitation.\n\nD. Visualize Execution\n\nIntegrate with my existing Code Flow Visualizer.\n\nWhen supported Python code is submitted for visualization:\n\nDisplay the actual executing line.\n\nTrack variable values.\n\nExplain conditions and loops.\n\nShow execution history.\n\nSupport Previous Step and Next Step.\n\nPreserve existing animations and beginner explanations.\n\nDo not create a duplicate execution engine unnecessarily.\n\nIf the existing visualizer cannot handle a particular Python construct, explain which construct is unsupported. Never fabricate execution steps or results.\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-27T15:32:05+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
