ion\": \"Step through the execution in the visualizer to inspect how variables mutate to produce the result.\"\r\n79:       }\r\n80:     ],\r\n81:     \"constraints\": [\r\n82:       \"1 <= nums.length <= 10^4\",\r\n83:       \"-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\",\r\n84:       \"Memory limit: 256 MB, Time limit: 2.0 seconds\"\r\n85:     ],\r\n86:  \n<truncated 1669 bytes>\ns\": [\r\n119:       {\r\n120:         \"input\": \"isAnagram(\\\"anagram\\\", \\\"nagaram\\\")\",\r\n121:         \"output\": \"Computed via isAnagram(\\\"anagram\\\", \\\"nagaram\\\")\",\r\n122:         \"explanation\": \"Step through the execution in the visualizer to inspect how variables mutate to produce the result.\"\r\n123:       }\r\n124:     ],\r\n125:     \"constraints\": [\r\n126:       \"1 <= nums.length <= 10^4\",\r\n127:       \"-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4\",\r\n128:       \"Memory limit: 256 MB, Time limit: 2.0 seconds\"\r\n129:     ],\r\n130:     \"prerequisites\": [\r\n131:       \"Array Indexing & Iteration\",\r\n132:       \"String Manipulation\",\r\n133:       \"Hash Map / Dict Key Lookup\"\r\n134:     ],\r\n135:     \"referenceSolution\": \"def isAnagram(s, t):\\n    if len(s) != len(t):\\n        return False\\n    countS = {}\\n    countT = {}\\n    for ch in s:\\n        countS[ch] = countS.get(ch, 0) + 1\\n    for ch in t:\\n        countT[ch] = countT.get(ch, 0) + 1\\n    return countS == countT\\n\\nprint(\\\"Is anagram:\\\", isAnagram(\\\"anagram\\\", \\\"nagaram\\\"))\",\r\n136:     \"verificationStatus\": \"Verified\"\r\n137:   },\r\n138:   {\r\n139:     \"id\": 4,\r\n140:     \"leetcodeNumber\": 49,\r\n141:     \"title\": \"Group Anagrams\",\r\n142:     \"difficulty\": \"Medium\",\r\n143:     \"topic\": \"Arrays & Hashing\",\r\n144:     \"pattern\": \"Categorization by Key\",\r\n145:     \"description\": \"Group strings that are anagrams together by sorting or frequency tuple keys.\",\r\n146:     \"timeComplexity\": \"O(m * n log n)\",\r\n147:     \"spaceComplexity\": \"O(m * n)\",\r\n148:     \"starterCode\": \"def groupAnagrams(strs):\\n    ansMap = {}\\n    for s in strs:\\n        key = \\\"\\\".join(sorted(s))\\n        if key not in ansMap:\\n            ansMap[key] = []\\n        ansMap[key].append(s)\\n    return list(ansMap.values())\\n\\nprint(\\\"Groups:\\\", groupAnagrams([\\\"eat\\\", \\\"tea\\\", \\\"tan\\\", \\\"ate\\\", \\\"nat\\\", \\\"bat\\\"]))\",\r\n149:     \"topics\": [\r\n150:       \"Arrays\",\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
